6. Automated validation & scoring

Use deterministic checks:

Does the generated definition mention the subject (customer/account) inferred from tokens?

Does unit/type match sample data?

Check for contradictions vs. existing glossary.


Build a confidence score combining:

Token-match score (how many expanded tokens are in the definition)

Embedding similarity between generated definition and retrieved docs

LLM self-assigned confidence or consistency across multiple model runs

Rule-based match (1 if rule and LLM agree)


Example simple formula:

score = 0.4 * token_match + 0.4 * doc_similarity + 0.2 * agreement_with_rules



